== Q4 | Equilibrium for Dragontear (B3.1, B4.1)

Use a graph to describe the market for Dragontear:

#grid(
  columns: (2fr, 1fr),
  gutter: 1em,
  [
    a) Calculate equilibrium price: *40* Find equilibrium quantity: *200* (B3.1)

    b) At 30 coins: *shortage*, excess of size *150*, and the price will: *rise*, fall (B3.1)

    c) Calculate total surplus at equilibrium: *6000* (B4.1)

    d) What is the deadweight loss if only 100 vials are exchanged? *1500* (B4.1)
  ],
  [
    #image("data:image/svg+xml;base64,", width: 100%)
  ],
)

#block(width: 100%, stroke: (left: 2pt + rgb("#c00000")), inset: (left: 1em))[
  #set text(fill: rgb("#c00000"))

  a) 60 − Q/10 = Q/5 gives 60 = 3Q/10, so Q\* = *200* and P\* = *40*.

  b) At 30, Qd = 300 and Qs = 150: a *shortage* of *150*. The price will *rise*: buyers who miss out bid it up, and sellers respond with more vials, until the gap closes at 40.

  c) TS = CS + PS = ½ · 200 · (60 − 40) + ½ · 200 · 40 = 2000 + 4000 = *6000*, or the whole triangle between the curves, ½ · 200 · 60.

  d) At Q = 100, MB = 50 and MC = 20. The trades from 100 to 200 are worth making, since MB is above MC on each one, and their lost surplus is the triangle DWL = ½ · (50 − 20) · (200 − 100) = *1500*.

]

